next_action:
  id: GATE-A-ASSESSMENT
  description_es: Evaluar conjuntamente AR-1, AR-2 y AR-3 para determinar si Phase I puede cerrarse y habilitar Phase II — Reconstruction Semantics.
  description_en: Jointly assess AR-1, AR-2 and AR-3 to determine whether Phase I can close and enable Phase II — Reconstruction Semantics.
  decision_target: GATE_A_PASS_REWORK_OR_FAIL

gate_a_checks:
  - Boundary Model closed and coherent
  - Representation Model closed and neutral
  - Binding Model closed and authority-safe
  - AR-1/AR-2/AR-3 semantic interfaces coherent
  - no circular authority/dependency introduced
  - KOS-specific realization remains outside neutral core
  - non-KOS realization conceptually feasible
  - reconstruction remains outside Phase I ownership
  - encoding remains outside Phase I ownership
  - KCP remains outside Phase I ownership
  - residual risks are non-blocking for Phase II

reentry_rule:
  - verify actual Git HEAD before development
  - reconcile CURRENT.kscl against later commits/documents
  - do not infer authority from this record

assertions:
  - CURRENT.kscl is mutable continuity state
  - checkpoint is historical snapshot
  - KSCL continuity != architectural authority
  - KSCL reconstruction != proof
